WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.319 --> 00:00:04.910
What's up guys my name is Colin McNeil for
theScore esports.

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:08.179
Great commentary can elevate play in any
esport.

00:00:08.179 --> 00:00:15.349
Turning the memorable into the unforgettable.
Making a good play into one that's iconic.

00:00:15.349 --> 00:00:21.220
And nowhere is this more evident
than in the fighting game and Smash Bros.communities.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:32.340
(Casting)

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:33.700
Yeeeaaah.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:37.500
Ao anyways get your bionic arm out
and your Haagen Dazs scoops ready, because

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:43.460
we're doing the top 10 FGC and
Smash Bros. commentator calls.

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:49.180
Oh and right before we get into it guys, I'm gonna need
you to hit that YouTube wombo combo. That means hit subscribe,

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:51.320
like and do leave a comment.

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:59.291
Kicking off our list at number 10 is UltraDavid’s
iconic “Bionic Arm!” call

00:00:59.291 --> 00:01:01.700
at Final Round 14.

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:09.560
It was Marvel vs. Capcom 3 winners’ semifinals and Combofiend
managed to claw his way back from the brink

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:13.020
of defeat with his final remaining character,
Spencer.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:18.270
With a magic pixel of health, his Spencer
holds on for dear life, melting Marn’s Zero

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:25.000
and Sentinel and setting the stage for UltraDavid
to yell those famous words.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:48.780
(Casting)

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:52.900
Coming in at number nine is D1 and his super fighting robot call.

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:59.740
During the Super Smash Bros. Invitational
at E3 2014, HugS released his Mega Man's final

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:04.000
smash, sending D1 into an absolute frenzy.

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:24.680
(Casting)

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:31.580
Making its way in at number 8 on our list is Bronson Tran at NCR 2017

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:37.580
Tran had the unique experience of commentating
his own matches at the NorCal Regionals 2017

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:38.580
Top 8.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:41.000
He took the opportunity and ran with it.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:03:25.520
(Casting)

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:28.760
Oh and by the way, he won the entire tournament too.

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:44.000
(Casting)

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:51.560
Number seven in our list is the call behind
Tokido’s infamous taunt combo at EVO 2017.

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:56.480
Sajam and James Chen were on the desk for
Street Fighter 5’s emotionally charged Grand

00:03:56.480 --> 00:04:02.870
Finals, which featured a matchup between FGC
legend Tokido and rising star Punk.

00:04:02.870 --> 00:04:08.250
In Game 1, Tokido styled on Punk like no one
had ever seen before.

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:14.590
We could describe the round for you, the surprise,
the shock and awe -- but honestly, no one

00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:17.000
could have put it better than Sajam.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:30.100
(Casting)

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:35.560
At number six we have Hellpockets
and Metaphysics at EVO 2017.

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:41.650
The King of Fighters 14 grand final saw E.T.’s
Daimon versus Xiaohai’s Iori, and featured

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:47.000
a perfectly timed Seismic Wave, plus one unforgettable
call.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:05:00.000
(Casting)

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:06.440
At number five, we have SkiSonic and Yipes  crowning Marvel Vs Capcom’s returning

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:07.710
monarch.

00:05:07.710 --> 00:05:14.200
Justin Wong and ChrisG went punch for punch,
until Justin popped off, reuniting himself

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:17.000
with the Marvel vs. Capcom throne.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:06:02.000
(Casting)

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:03.860
You knew this one was coming.

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:11.640
An FGC commentary list just wouldn’t be
complete without Yipes and his brilliant stream

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:17.000
of consciousness Mahvel calls at Seasons Beatings
2. Oh he’s so pringles!

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:44.460
(Casting)

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:49.660
Unlike some of the other moments from this
Top 10, this Marvel vs Capcom 2 match, could

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:51.670
have been lost to time.

00:06:51.670 --> 00:06:56.310
That is, if it wasn't for Yipes coming through
with one of the funniest, most memorable,

00:06:56.310 --> 00:07:00.000
and quotable commentary in FGC history.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:05.880
(Casting)

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:09.000
At number three, we have the Wombo Combo.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:15.560
Phil, Mango, and HomeMadeWaffles were commentating the Loser’s semifinal at the SCSA West

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:20.590
Coast Circuit when SilentSpectre and Tang
decided to juggle Zhu.

00:07:20.590 --> 00:07:25.000
What followed, was a call that would go on
to become an internet phenomenon….

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:49.500
(Casting)

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:55.780
Coming in at number two we have now iconic
commentary behind the Wong Factor comeback.

00:07:55.780 --> 00:08:01.650
Facing off against Yipes at EVO 2007, Justin
Wong made an unforgettable comeback with only

00:08:01.650 --> 00:08:04.150
his anchor, Cyclops, still standing.

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:09.060
It’s only fitting that one of the biggest
rallies in FGC history was complemented by

00:08:09.060 --> 00:08:12.000
one of the hypest casting calls of all time.

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:29.100
(Casting)

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:37.380
Capping off our list at number one, is one
of the most memorable calls in all of esports, let alone fighting games.

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:43.280
A play that has been shown on ESPN’s Sportscenter
and made mainstream headlines around the internet.

00:08:43.289 --> 00:08:50.339
At the Guilty Gear Xrd winner’s semis at
EVO 2015, Woshige made a very costly mistake

00:08:50.339 --> 00:08:53.200
in celebrating one round too early.

00:08:53.200 --> 00:09:28.680
(Casting)

00:09:28.840 --> 00:09:33.700
Not only was the moment hella embarrassing
for Woshige, commentators Hellpockets and

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:38.480
Ryan Hunter famously scolded him for his premature
celebration.

00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:43.600
(Casting)

